<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Yes Full power Samething unfortunatly. But with original firmware no problem, 10W<br><br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi !<br><br>I get a strange behaviour with my DMR transmission on some repeater. My radio is RT-90 v.1<br>I test with the BM parrot. (tested with real QSO also)<br>My RSSI signal is good and similar on both repeater.<br><br>I tested the last firmware with a local repeater here, a Motorola SLR8000. My audio is scattered, missing some syllables, not really usable.<br>If i try with the original firmware, the audio is perfect.<br><br>I try another local repeater, a Hytera RD982S. This time the audio (of my transmission) is perfect! I also try with my Hotspot and no problem.<br><br>There is a compatibility issue with some kind of repeater like Motorola ? There is something I can do to improve it ?<br><br>Thanks 73 !!<br>VE2DKA</div></blockquote>IIRC the early MD9600 have a problem with the PA response time.<br><br>Did you try running full power, as that was the workaround</div></blockquote><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5359">ve2dka</a> — Tue Feb 04, 2025 7:08 pm</p><hr />
